ritten before reboot was readable afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed cryptsetup on node1\",\"Generated a 4096-byte random keyfile at /etc/luks-keys/secure.key (mode 400, root:root)\",\"Created a 2GiB sparse backing file /var/lib/luks-volumes/secure.img and formatted it as LUKS2 using the keyfile\",\"Opened the LUKS container as /dev/mapper/secure and formatted it XFS\",\"Added /etc/crypttab entry (secure, backing file, keyfile, luks,nofail) so systemd-cryptsetup-generator auto-unlocks it at boot\",\"Added /etc/fstab entry (UUID=..., /srv/secure, xfs, defaults,nofail) so it auto-mounts at boot\",\"Verified manual mount, wrote a test file, then unmounted/closed and re-triggered via systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service to simulate boot path\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, mount state, cryptsetup status, test file contents)\",\"Rebooted node1 via systemd-run scheduled reboot, returning the ack before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again and confirmed boot_id changed\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: /srv/secure mounted, cryptsetup status active, test file readable, relevant systemd units active\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Encrypted volume exists and is mounted at /srv/secure, backed by cryptsetup/LUKS\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5b499e6672ee4469\",\"cmd-c1beb59a05364c94\"],\"summary\":\"cryptsetup installed; LUKS2 container created on a file, opened as /dev/mapper/secure, formatted XFS, and mounted at /srv/secure with test file written and read back\"},{\"requirement\":\"Volume unlocks and mounts automatically at boot (no manual intervention)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c1beb59a05364c94\"],\"summary\":\"crypttab/fstab entries added; after manual close, triggering systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service (the same unit systemd runs at boot) auto-unlocked the volume and it mounted per fstab, with test file intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-229d0b4cdcc9414a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id d052eb57-c81d-4309-ae7f-bce362073ff9, active mount, active LUKS mapping, and readable test file before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-02975a7f4d634afb\"],\"summary\":\"systemd-run scheduled a delayed reboot and the ack ('reboot scheduled') returned successfully before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof node1 actually restarted (changed boot identity)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-99e8f3eb0c514e6d\",\"cmd-22191d6d7f42405d\",\"cmd-542706361da94570\",\"cmd-165fee89ef6048c1\"],\"summary\":\"Connection dropped during reboot, node was unreachable for several poll attempts, then came back with boot_id f8b3e503-df03-4a7d-8286-5087c4cdd521 (different from baseline) and uptime since 08:10:09\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of encrypted volume, data, and service state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3b275eaed67443be\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/secure is mounted from /dev/mapper/secure, cryptsetup status shows active LUKS2 mapping, test file content 'hello-encrypted' still present, and systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service is active — all without manual intervention\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created a LUKS2-encrypted file-backed volume on node1 mounted at /srv/secure, configured to auto-unlock (via a root-only keyfile referenced in /etc/crypttab) and auto-mount (via /etc/fstab) at boot with no manual intervention. Verified across a full node reboot: boot_id changed, systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service and the fstab mount both came up active automatically, and the test file written before reboot was readable afterward.","actions_performed":["Installed cryptsetup on node1","Generated a 4096-byte random keyfile at /etc/luks-keys/secure.key (mode 400, root:root)","Created a 2GiB sparse backing file /var/lib/luks-volumes/secure.img and formatted it as LUKS2 using the keyfile","Opened the LUKS container as /dev/mapper/secure and formatted it XFS","Added /etc/crypttab entry (secure, backing file, keyfile, luks,nofail) so systemd-cryptsetup-generator auto-unlocks it at boot","Added /etc/fstab entry (UUID=..., /srv/secure, xfs, defaults,nofail) so it auto-mounts at boot","Verified manual mount, wrote a test file, then unmounted/closed and re-triggered via systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service to simulate boot path","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, mount state, cryptsetup status, test file contents)","Rebooted node1 via systemd-run scheduled reboot, returning the ack before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec was available again and confirmed boot_id changed","Verified post-restart recovery: /srv/secure mounted, cryptsetup status active, test file readable, relevant systemd units active"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume exists and is mounted at /srv/secure, backed by cryptsetup/LUKS","command_ids":["cmd-5b499e6672ee4469","cmd-c1beb59a05364c94"],"summary":"cryptsetup installed; LUKS2 container created on a file, opened as /dev/mapper/secure, formatted XFS, and mounted at /srv/secure with test file written and read back"},{"requirement":"Volume unlocks and mounts automatically at boot (no manual intervention)","command_ids":["cmd-c1beb59a05364c94"],"summary":"crypttab/fstab entries added; after manual close, triggering systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service (the same unit systemd runs at boot) auto-unlocked the volume and it mounted per fstab, with test file intact"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1","command_ids":["cmd-229d0b4cdcc9414a"],"summary":"Captured boot_id d052eb57-c81d-4309-ae7f-bce362073ff9, active mount, active LUKS mapping, and readable test file before reboot"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-02975a7f4d634afb"],"summary":"systemd-run scheduled a delayed reboot and the ack ('reboot scheduled') returned successfully before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Proof node1 actually restarted